\title{ShinyCEA: Shiny Application for Cost-Effectiveness Analysis}
\description{
An R package with a Shiny application designed for teaching and applied research in cost-effectiveness analysis (CEA). Supports multiple model structures (e.g., Markov, Partitioned Survival) and allows analysts to perform deterministic and probabilistic evaluations. Features include parameter upload/editing, sensitivity analyses (DSA/PSA), publication-ready plots (Tornado, CE Plane, Frontier, CEAC), downloadable results, and automated report generation. Users can plug in custom models with minimal code via the new_cea_model() interface.
